# Next.js App Rules

- Preserve existing URLs, metadata, content, and visual behavior.
- Use Server Components by default.
- Add `"use client"` only when client-side state, effects, browser APIs, or event handlers are required.
- Keep reusable UI in `components/`.
- Keep page-specific content and logic close to the relevant route.
- Use Next.js `Image` for optimized images when appropriate.
- Use `Link` for internal navigation.
- Keep secrets and private environment variables server-side.
- Use environment variables for configuration; never hardcode credentials.
- Ensure pages remain accessible, responsive, and SEO-friendly.
